  "purpose": "Machine-readable terminal-claim registry for the RELEASE-01 Proof-Carrying Interop V2 §38 contract. This is the terminal layer above the WORD (LAB-01), GOOGLE (GOOGLE-01), MULTI-01 and CAPABILITY_MATRIX contours: it binds every public Word/DOCX product wording string (README.md, package.json description, src/menu/menu-config.v2.json labels, src/renderer/editor.js formatting/status strings) to a typed claim, a profile class and committed evidence, and records NOT_CLAIMED_BLOCKED claims for the Google profiles, Windows Word, Word Online, the MULTI_SCENE_COORDINATOR blocked row and the (not-yet-made) Word saturation claim. The wordingSurfaces sha256 values are the exact file sha256 at registry authoring time; every claimDigest is a stable sorted-keys sha256 over the claim minus its own claimDigest. The terminalNonClaimInventory is the deduplicated union of the real source nonClaim inventories (both Google profiles, CAPABILITY_MATRIX top-level nonClaims, the Word normalized-matrix nonClaims) plus the two terminal non-claims WORD_MAC_16_111_2_COMPLETE_NOT_SATURATED and MULTI_SCENE_ATOMIC_APPLY_BLOCKED_UNTIL_DECISIVE_CRASH_PROOF. The terminal roll-up stays NOT_MADE_WORD_TERMINAL_PASS_REQUIRED: Word 16.111.2-d1 is COMPETING_NOT_SATURATED (not SATURATED), both Google profiles are DECLARED, the MULTI_SCENE_COORDINATOR row remains blocked, and Windows/Online Word are unproven. This registry is read-only evidence; it grants no product write authority and never changes Word or Google saturation status.",
